WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.620 --> 00:00:05.799
Justice League may have been released almost
two years ago back in November 2017, but there's

00:00:05.800 --> 00:00:08.020
still plenty of mystique surrounding the film.

00:00:08.420 --> 00:00:13.320
Director Zack Snyder suddenly left Justice
League in May 2017 as post-production was

00:00:13.339 --> 00:00:17.760
about to start, deciding to stay home and
support his family after the death of his

00:00:17.760 --> 00:00:18.480
daughter, Autumn.

00:00:19.000 --> 00:00:22.820
Into the void stepped Avengers director Joss
Whedon to complete the film.

00:00:22.900 --> 00:00:27.260
But according to those who worked on the movie,
he didn't exactly pick up where Snyder left

00:00:27.260 --> 00:00:30.240
off, making drastic changes to the final product.

00:00:30.600 --> 00:00:35.780
The theatrical version of Justice League resulted
in mixed reviews, but then came hope for DC

00:00:35.789 --> 00:00:40.969
fans in the form of the newsflash that Snyder,
despite his departure from the film before

00:00:40.969 --> 00:00:43.720
completion, still has his version of Justice
League.

00:00:44.140 --> 00:00:49.199
That juicy little tidbit has had DC fans'
tongues wagging, eager to see what has been

00:00:49.200 --> 00:00:50.480
dubbed "the Snyder Cut."

00:00:51.060 --> 00:00:55.460
It's been a long time waiting for an update
on that cut, and while it seems increasingly

00:00:55.460 --> 00:00:59.940
unlikely the cut will ever be released to
the public, there are some in higher circles

00:00:59.940 --> 00:01:01.960
who have been lucky enough to lay eyes on
it.

00:01:02.460 --> 00:01:07.620
Jason Momoa, who starred in Justice League
as the underwater superhero Aquaman, is one

00:01:07.620 --> 00:01:08.980
of that very elite group.

00:01:09.480 --> 00:01:14.550
To Momoa's Instagram followers, this is old
news, because the Aquaman star revealed back

00:01:14.550 --> 00:01:18.480
in August that the "Snyder Cut" was, quote,
"ssssiiicccckkkkkk."

00:01:18.800 --> 00:01:24.360
Earlier this month, Momoa was speaking to
MTV News' Josh Horowitz when he revealed maybe

00:01:24.360 --> 00:01:27.460
a bit more than Warner Bros. executives will
be pleased with.

00:01:27.840 --> 00:01:32.600
When Horowitz brought up a past comment Momoa
made about the Snyder Cut of Justice League

00:01:32.600 --> 00:01:33.280
that being…

00:01:33.600 --> 00:01:35.060
"F—- yeah, I need to see that."

00:01:35.220 --> 00:01:36.940
Momoa dropped this bombshell:

00:01:37.260 --> 00:01:38.260
"Yeah, absolutely.

00:01:38.500 --> 00:01:39.660
But I have seen it, so…"

00:01:39.820 --> 00:01:40.660
"You've seen —"

00:01:40.660 --> 00:01:41.860
"I've seen the Snyder Cut."

00:01:42.440 --> 00:01:47.620
Though Snyder left Justice League before post-production
started, Momoa seemed to hint that Snyder

00:01:47.620 --> 00:01:52.440
may in fact have completed his original vision
for the film effects and all.

00:01:52.620 --> 00:01:57.480
After Momoa revealed he's already seen the
Snyder Cut, Horowitz posed the question:

00:01:57.860 --> 00:01:59.310
So what does that mean?

00:01:59.310 --> 00:02:01.020
Because the effects aren't done.

00:02:01.020 --> 00:02:05.240
You've seen his assemblage of footage and
alternate takes?"

00:02:05.240 --> 00:02:06.840
Only for Momoa to quip back:

00:02:07.320 --> 00:02:10.000
“Oh, you think he — Zack couldn't finish
it?"

00:02:10.240 --> 00:02:14.900
The actor didn't let too much slip though,
following with a quick "next question!" when

00:02:14.920 --> 00:02:18.980
Horowitz tried to get confirmation about whether
the Snyder Cut is fully edited.

00:02:19.380 --> 00:02:24.000
Despite the secrecy surrounding the cut, Momoa
does feel that it's worth making it available

00:02:24.020 --> 00:02:24.660
to the public.

00:02:24.840 --> 00:02:29.900
Momoa's also hoping his statements don't get
him fired from Aquaman 2, the sequel to his

00:02:29.900 --> 00:02:33.240
surprise smash-hit standalone from December
2018.

00:02:33.700 --> 00:02:38.180
Let's recap: The final cut of Justice League
that was ultimately released to the public

00:02:38.189 --> 00:02:43.560
in November 2017 wasn't very well received,
with fans saying they could clearly see where

00:02:43.560 --> 00:02:46.500
one director's vision ended and the other's
began.

00:02:46.860 --> 00:02:51.180
According to The Wrap, the incomplete look
of Justice League spurred an insider to give

00:02:51.180 --> 00:02:54.380
it the unfortunate description of "a Frankenstein"
film.

00:02:54.830 --> 00:02:58.920
Sources with knowledge of the production have
also revealed that approximately 30 minutes

00:02:58.930 --> 00:03:03.189
of the released film was actually directed
by Whedon, replacing 30 minutes of filming

00:03:03.189 --> 00:03:05.020
done by Snyder the first time around.

00:03:05.520 --> 00:03:09.780
That doesn't include footage shot by Snyder
that Whedon edited into a completely different

00:03:09.780 --> 00:03:11.380
context for the final product.

00:03:11.500 --> 00:03:16.279
Whedon, who is known for his work in the Marvel
Cinematic Universe, managed to disappoint

00:03:16.280 --> 00:03:22.060
DC fans as he tried to incorporate misplaced
humor into an altogether darker universe.

00:03:22.260 --> 00:03:26.840
Followers of the franchise are thrilled there's
another version of Justice League, and have

00:03:26.840 --> 00:03:29.160
been calling desperately for it to be released.

00:03:29.310 --> 00:03:34.000
The hashtag "ReleaseTheSnyderCut" has been
doing the rounds on social media with a petition

00:03:34.019 --> 00:03:39.629
started as early as the film's release in
November 2017, and efforts only amped up after

00:03:39.629 --> 00:03:42.920
Momoa confirmed its existence in October 2018.

00:03:43.240 --> 00:03:49.120
Momoa's recent remarks to MTV News only add
fuel to this ever-burning fire… a fire which

00:03:49.120 --> 00:03:54.129
has also been stoked by the likes of Justice
League cinematographer Fabian Wagner and Jesse

00:03:54.129 --> 00:03:59.540
Eisenberg and Ray Fisher, the actors who portrayed
Lex Luthor and Cyborg respectively.

00:03:59.820 --> 00:04:03.260
All three have stated that they'd like to
see the Snyder Cut released to the public.

00:04:03.780 --> 00:04:07.840
Though Warner Bros. is remaining tight-lipped
at this stage about the Snyder Cut of Justice

00:04:07.840 --> 00:04:11.120
League, the excitement surrounding it sure
isn't dying down.

00:04:11.560 --> 00:04:15.639
With little details being leaked here and
there, the studio might one day be persuaded

00:04:15.640 --> 00:04:19.040
to let the heroes loose as they were originally
intended.

